Well, I've never managed to let my yeomen live long, but...

One of the great pet to ride, overall, is the kirin. Self-healing and good  
stats.
The usual problem with the kirin, however, is that it doesn't eat, meaning  
that you won't be able to retame it if it ever becomes untame (high MR  
also). This means that (un)mounting it too often will result in loosing  
the beast... I once had a ki-rin stead and lost it due to untaming :-(

With yeoman, you have a "calm stead" technique that allow to tame your  
stead. My plans when playing a yeoman are always to wish for a figurine of  
a kirin and try to ride it 'til the end. (never mangaged it)

I don't know whether it's a good strategy, but at least it would be pretty  
cool :-)

